From: AdobeWine
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: GetVolumeInformationW accepts a mounted folder as the root.

GetVolumePathNameW returns a Unix mount point inside a drive as the volume (Z:\m2\ for /m2 on its own file system),
as Windows does for a mounted folder, but GetVolumeInformationW took only a drive root (exactly one backslash) and
failed such a path with ERROR_DIR_NOT_ROOT. Windows accepts a mounted folder there. Lightroom Classic asks for the
volume of the export folder this way and, when the second call fails, gives up the export with "The file could not
be written" before it renders anything; every export to a folder on such a mount failed (to C: it worked). A path
that GetVolumePathNameW reports as a volume root is now opened as a directory and queried by handle; other subfolders
still fail with ERROR_DIR_NOT_ROOT.
Test: wine/tests/volpath (GetVolumePathNameW + GetVolumeInformationW): Z:\m2\ error 144 before, NTFS after;
Z:\m2\AdobeWine\ and C:\users\ still 144, C:\ and Z:\ unchanged.
Test: observer/scenarios/lightroom-classic/usage.sh with the work folder on Z:\m2 (own xfs mount): exports
14-18 "The file could not be written" before, all 18 tests and the 9 disk checks PASS after.
---
diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/volume.c b/dlls/kernelbase/volume.c
index edfd777..5b75a1a 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/volume.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/volume.c
@@ -162,6 +162,22 @@ BOOL WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH GetVolumeInformationW( LPCWSTR root, LPWSTR label,
     for (i = 4; i < nt_name.Length / sizeof(WCHAR); i++) if (nt_name.Buffer[i] == '\\') break;
     if (i != nt_name.Length / sizeof(WCHAR) - 1)
     {
+        WCHAR volume[MAX_PATH];
+
+        /* a mounted folder (GetVolumePathNameW returns Unix mount points inside a drive, e.g. Z:\m2\) is a
+         * volume root too, as on Windows */
+        if (nt_name.Buffer[nt_name.Length / sizeof(WCHAR) - 1] == '\\' &&
+            GetVolumePathNameW( root, volume, ARRAY_SIZE(volume) ) && !wcsicmp( volume, root ))
+        {
+            InitializeObjectAttributes( &attr, &nt_name, OBJ_CASE_INSENSITIVE, 0, NULL );
+            status = NtOpenFile( &handle, SYNCHRONIZE, &attr, &io, FILE_SHARE_READ | FILE_SHARE_WRITE,
+                                 FILE_DIRECTORY_FILE | FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_NONALERT );
+            if (!set_ntstatus( status )) goto done;
+            ret = GetVolumeInformationByHandleW( handle, label, label_len, serial, filename_len, flags,
+                                                 fsname, fsname_len );
+            NtClose( handle );
+            goto done;
+        }
         /* check if root contains an explicit subdir */
         if (root[0] && root[1] == ':') root += 2;
         while (*root == '\\') root++;
